WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.380
Sigourney Weaver is one of the most&nbsp;
esteemed actors working today — and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.640
for her latest role, she's playing a blue&nbsp;
teenage alien who’s 59 years younger than her.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.520
In creating the technicolor,&nbsp;
eye-popping world of Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.140
James Cameron looked to a different sort of space&nbsp;
epic. In an interview with Variety, he said:

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.620
"If you look at how George Lucas did it&nbsp;
in the universe that he created, [...] he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.220
chose to make each different biome, each&nbsp;
different culture, have their own planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.820
around the galaxy. And I thought, 'Well,&nbsp;
that's not the way Earth works.' I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.780
spend as many films as I want to make just on&nbsp;
Pandora, just by going to different places."

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.220
Cameron has begun to lift the curtain&nbsp;
on Pandora's cultural and biospheric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.820
diversity in Avatar: The Way of Water.&nbsp;
With so many new shores to explore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.360
it stands to reason that The Way of&nbsp;
Water carries a few unanswered questions.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.860
What is the fate of the forest-dwelling&nbsp;
Omaticaya people? What will happen to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.660
the tulkun? Why did James Cameron cast a&nbsp;
septuagenarian to play a 14-year-old? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.460
apparently that last question has been a&nbsp;
particular point of contention among Avatar fans.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.160
Sigourney Weaver made her first trip to Pandora in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.240
2009's Avatar, in which she played&nbsp;
exobiologist Dr. Grace Augustine.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:09.900
"I'm with her now, Jake. She's real."

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.680
Even though her character was killed,&nbsp;
Weaver nabbed an unlikely role in Avatar:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.880
The Way of Water as Kiri, the 14-year-old&nbsp;
adopted daughter of Jake and Neytiri.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.740
Kiri is one of the most important new characters&nbsp;
in the Avatar universe; the daughter of Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.900
Augustine, Kiri boasts a unique connection to&nbsp;
the environment and Eywa. Still, for some fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.660
casting a now-73-year-old actress as a teenager&nbsp;
was a bridge too far. One Twitter user wrote:

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.800
"It really didn't work at all. The&nbsp;
movie is great but it was so jarring."

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.120
Some thought that the unconventional casting&nbsp;
choice was a missed opportunity to lean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.760
into the themes of reincarnation. One person said:

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.780
"Sigourney Weaver playing Kiri was an&nbsp;
interesting idea and could lead to some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.960
solid world building with reincarnation&nbsp;
and the world tree and the like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.460
but the performance...IDK...I could really&nbsp;
see this was an adult trying to play a child."

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.260
Others still felt that Weaver's performance&nbsp;
felt naturally less youthful when sharing scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.380
with her younger cast mates, leading&nbsp;
her to stick out like a sore thumb.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.620
While teenage Sigourney Weaver took&nbsp;
some viewers out of the action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.240
others were deeply impressed by the actresses'&nbsp;
commitment to the role. One Redditor asked:

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.060
"⁠Is it wrong for me to want to&nbsp;
see more young Sigourney Weaver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.980
movies? She was awesome and killed it here."

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.600
One fan viewed Cameron's casting choice as&nbsp;
a win for older actors, especially women,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.700
who are frequently overlooked. They wrote:

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.320
"I honestly love James Cameron for this. We&nbsp;
have accepted way too much ageism in Hollywood."

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.540
Weaver's performance also won over some critics.&nbsp;
For Consequence, Liz Shannon Miller wrote:

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.780
"Weaver's performance actually proves&nbsp;
to be one of the film's high points.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.740
It's one of those 'damn, what can't she do?'&nbsp;
moments, watching her embody the character."

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:45.600
Ultimately, Weaver's greatest champion is James&nbsp;
Cameron himself. The director told Empire:

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.620
"Sigourney just became younger. She&nbsp;
looked younger, she had more energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.580
and she never quite stepped out of Kiri&nbsp;
for our whole capture period. She had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.160
glow on her face and lightness&nbsp;
in her step and a fun spirit."

